To solve $535^2 - 465^2$, we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that $a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)$. Here, $a = 535$ and $b = 465$.

First, calculate $(a - b)$:
\begin{align*}
a - b &= 535 - 465 \\
&= 70
\end{align*}

Next, calculate $(a + b)$:
\begin{align*}
a + b &= 535 + 465 \\
&= 1000
\end{align*}

Now apply the difference of squares formula:
\begin{align*}
535^2 - 465^2 &= (535 - 465)(535 + 465) \\
&= 70 \times 1000 \\
&= 70000
\end{align*}

Final answer: 70000
